+# The Daily Grind
+
+A static coffee homepage with a browser-based receipt and gift voucher signing workspace. No server or dependencies are needed for signing. Serve the files over HTTPS (or localhost) for Web Crypto access.
+
+## Usage
+
+- Choose a coffee and quantity, or fill in a gift voucher.
+- **Sign & download** creates a signed JSON file and verifies it before download.
+- **Verify a document** accepts a JSON file or pasted JSON and checks its signature against the signing identity saved in this browser.
+- **Download public key** exports the public JWK and its SHA-256 fingerprint; private keys cannot be exported.
+
+## Trust model
+
+ECDSA P-256 with SHA-256 signs the canonical JSON envelope, including document version, algorithm, key fingerprint, and all receipt or voucher fields. Verification rejects unsupported formats, unrecognized keys, invalid payloads, and changed signatures or content. JSON object key order does not affect verification.
+
+The non-exportable private CryptoKey and public key are saved in IndexedDB. Concurrent tabs share one identity. No private keys are sent to a service or bundled in the source. Storage failures disable signing rather than silently creating an ephemeral identity.
+
+This is a **local signing identity**, not a merchant issuance or payment system. A valid signature establishes that a document is unchanged and was signed by the corresponding saved browser key. It cannot establish that a merchant authorized a purchase or gift, that payment occurred, or that a voucher remains unredeemed. Documents from a different browser key are rejected. Clearing browser site data loses the signing identity. Production merchant issuance requires an independently trusted merchant public key, controlled merchant signing, and a payment/redemption service.
+
+Browser code running on this origin can request signing with the saved key. Keep the deployment and its scripts trusted; non-exportability does not protect against malicious same-origin code.
+
+Implementation uses the browser [Web Crypto signing API](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/SubtleCrypto/sign).
+
+## Automated checks
+
+Run `npm test` for valid receipt and voucher signatures, modified content and metadata, untrusted identities, non-exportable private keys, malformed documents, and canonical serialization. `node --check app.js` and `node --check signing.js` check JavaScript syntax. No build step is required.
